{
 "info": {
  "name": "MMG D:ONE \u2014 integration (0.5.5)",
  "description": "MMG D:ONE integration subset, firmware **0.5.5**. Stable. Stock on shelves.\n\nSource selection, quad multiview, media and playlist playback, output modes and device state. Network configuration, firmware updates, credential management and fleet features are deliberately excluded.\n\nSet `baseUrl` to the unit. There is no sign-in here: paste an OPERATOR service key into `apiKey` \u2014 make one on the unit, Settings > API keys. It is shown once, when you create it. The sign-ins return a session that expires, which is no use to something that has to still be working next month.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Selecting a source does NOT leave the quad or stop media playback. To cut to a single source, POST /api/quad/enable {\"enabled\": false} first. Only GET /api/snapshot reports what is actually on the screen.\n\nThis is a subset, not the whole API. The unit serves more than is collected here \u2014 what is left out is what a control surface has no business doing. If you need something that is not in this collection, ask us: support@mmgaxis.io.\n\nGenerated by generate.py \u2014 do not hand-edit.",
  "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
 },
 "auth": {
  "type": "bearer",
  "bearer": [
   {
    "key": "token",
    "value": "{{apiKey}}",
    "type": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "variable": [
  {
   "key": "baseUrl",
   "value": "",
   "description": "REQUIRED. The unit, with scheme and no trailing slash \u2014 http://192.168.1.23, or http://MMG-D1-XXXXXXXX.local using the serial printed on the box. Settings > Device on the unit shows both."
  },
  {
   "key": "apiKey",
   "value": "",
   "description": "REQUIRED. An OPERATOR service key, made on the unit: Settings > API keys. Operator reaches everything in this collection and cannot reconfigure the network or reset the device. A key lasts until you revoke it."
  }
 ],
